From 2042f8fa5cbdcba4aebc7b46797660969d0c64e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:06:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/17] generate: STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP=1 reads a batch
 admission's prompt beside the pipelined slot groups, BYIELD_NODRAIN condition
 (STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP, our c7e8fe1e 377f1b33 74a3b4f2 c6939188 90909f7c
 89dcda9e 9e64a578)

Production's final form of the overlapped read (c7e8fe1e .. 90909f7c), without STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_MAX_QUEUE
(56690405, 7fcea102: dropped), the spec lanes' parts (ee403737, P10), READ_YIELD's hook (P11) and STRATA_READS.
Same envs and defaults: STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP, _PRIO (default 1), _MTP_PRIO, _PLE_RESERVE (16), _SLEEP_US (20),
_JOIN_S (30), the test knobs _FORCE_PADUP / _FORCE_WAIT / _TEST_FAULT=poll|throw|stage|stall|cuda; the same log lines
("overlapped read off: <why>", "overlapped read: captured N group layouts", "overlapped read of N tokens in ...").

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- The hook moved from read_part's top to just before upstream's STRATA_PIPED_CONCURRENT block (after give_way): the
  segment's --prefill-pipe chunk plan is made first, and the read thread forces it (sp.force_chunk) before sp.run as
  read_part's own runs do, so an overlapped read reads the same chunks as the serial one. When our gate refuses, the
  segment goes on to upstream's paths unchanged (PIPED_CONCURRENT, PIECE, the pieces). With STRATA_PIPED_CONCURRENT=1
  too, ours goes first; said once.
- overlap_gate also refuses STRATA_PIPED_MTP (pmtp: proposal rows, deferred commits - no plain group layouts),
  waiting co-reads (STRATA_COALESCE_PREFILL: co_run parks, zeroes and syncs the device) and layer-major prefill
  (prefill_layer_major_resolve, default off on our cards). None of them is set in production.
- overlap_prepare calls upstream's mtp.reserve_prefill (instead of our reserve_prefill_records) and sp.reserve_uploads
  (#31's lesson: the prompt path's pinned upload ring, new since 0.1.44, would grow on the read thread), both for the
  buffers' chunk; a reserve_uploads failure is logged, as upstream's concurrent read does.
- read_overlapped sets upstream's in_prompt_read with ov_active (pa_due's prompt_read, the async tier, the watchdog's
  busy flag), calls share_gate() before the thread starts, and notes a KVA floor after a read from 0 as the run lambda
  does. The rows/D_ref stats use upstream's never-reset pipe_rows (our ov_rows is gone).
- pump: upstream's all-idle block (P4 timing, pc counters, PIPE_ADAPT_EVERY text, PIPED_MTP counts, SLOT_PARK waits)
  is factored unchanged into idle_report(reset_busy); pump calls it only without an overlapped read, read_overlapped
  after its drain with reset_busy false. The pick loop tests ov_layout first; SLOT_PARK's pad-row wait uses the
  overlapped width again (slot_park_blocks(gi, ov_active ? ov_S : 0), 9e64a578, reduced to 0 in the P4 port).
- F6: upstream's STRATA_PIPE_BYIELD_NODRAIN (a62bd38e) lacked `pipe_overlap_env() ||` in the main loop's drain
  condition; re-added with production's comment. The STRATA_TRACE drain timing (d8e371d5, upstream bc761d06) stays.
- Upstream's PleTable already locks every entry (a2de7446); STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP's setter block now only lets the
  reads leave that lock, queues the windows' rows as urgent and keeps the reserve.
- tools/batch_overlap_test.py: production's file (74a3b4f2 + c6939188). Its protocol (BT, BDONE, DONE field 5,
  RESUME, BADM, ERR) and the log lines it checks are unchanged in v0.2.12; batch_test.Engine is the same.

Not changed by v0.2.12 for this, noted for the identity runs: the v0.2.12 FP16 W16 weight cache (auto-on with
--batch >= 2) may cudaMalloc on the read thread on a card with more than its 3 GiB reserve free (a stall, never a
wrong value); on the production cards (1.3-1.4 GiB free) it turns itself off at its first try. Keep
STRATA_PF_W16_CACHE_MIB=0 in identity runs.

STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP unset: every new branch is behind pipe_overlap_env() (or ov_active, false), idle_report(true) runs
upstream's block at upstream's place, and the F6 condition reduces to upstream's.

Checked: generate.cpp passes -fsyntax-only with the integration build's flags (only the warnings it had before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
